Change SIGs:

What are SIGs?

  A SIG stands for Special Interest Group. The VBBS message system is fairly
  unique in its setup. Instead of residing on the host BBS, the message base
  resides on YOUR system.

  WHY, you might ask? Stephen Vermeulen's belief is that the message base on
  your system will become a library of messages, a valuable source of
  information. I agree with him. How many times have you read something
  from one of the many BBSs you call, but can't find the message or just
  cannot remember what the entire message said. Maybe your newsletter could
  use a review that you saw on USENET, but there is no way you're
  going to go back through a hundred messages a day to find that
  review or for that matter a thousand messages a week ago.

  So why not store these messages on your system. You only need to PROTECT/
  KEEP/ARCHIVE the messages you wish to keep and the rest are removed from
  your system (by running AGE). Using the time filter you will be able to
  go back in time and reread/'cut out' those messages you wish to reference.

  NOTE: In the fairly near future, a number of features will be added to
        VBBSReader to allow you to add keywords to your PROTECTED messages.

        Using another utility you will be able to 'collect' these messages
        in groups and combine them into an even more useful reference.

        For example:

          A message about a 3D shuttle Imagine object from XYZ BBS comes
          in. You feel it's worth while to keep. You assign: Imagine, 3D
          Object, Ray Tracing, Shuttle and XYZ BBS to the message.

          Later on you wish to access all messages to do with Imagine.
          You simply indicate Imagine in the search criteria and select
          commit. A time later (you will be able to do other things
          while the search is being done) all messages matching the
          search criteria will have been collected and will be
          available for viewing.

  After a number of months collecting messages, you will find yourself with
  a fairly impressive library of messages.

  This is the philosophy behind the VBBS message system and a quick look
  into the future. Now let's get into setting up your SIGs.

Handling SIGs:

  The VBBS BBS you call will have a number of message areas set up (we'll
  call them SIGs). You may or may not wish to read all the SIG areas. To
  be able to modify this list of SIGs, you must have logged onto the VBBS
  BBS and selected SIGs from the main panel. This will automatically
  send you the complete list of SIGs. You will notice messages will be
  sent to you. Don't worry, you won't be getting ALL the messages. Your
  SYSOP will have setup a small number of default SIGs that you will
  get. It might take 10 to 20 minutes to get these messages, so go do
  something else on VBBS. :-)

  Once you get the "SIG Complete" message, then you can close down SIGs.
  (remember this is from the Term program you will be doing the above).

  You can now run READ/VBBSReader (experiment with both of them, decide
  which one you like to use) and be able to see the messages you have
  just downloaded.

  To remove/add SIGs to these 2 or 3 defaults, just select Change SIGs
  from the main VBBSMenu panel. A list of BBSs will be displayed. If you
  have only logged onto one system, only one will be shown. If you have
  logged onto a number of systems, each of the BBSs will be listed.

  Select one of them by single clicking on the one you wish to change.

  A large window will appear with two lists. The one on the left is the
  WHOLE list of SIGs found on THAT BBS. The list on the right is which
  SIGs you are currently getting messages for.

  NOTE: When you first start up, you will find that ALL of the SIGs are on
        the right and there aren't any on the left. By selecting the
        'unwanted' SIGs you will notice they will disappear from the right
        side and reappear on the left. When you do this, that message base
        will NOT be downloaded. Of course if you select the SIG on the
        left side again it will reappear on the right and messages
        associated with that SIG will be downloaded to your system.

  By selecting a SIG from either side you will see it disappear from the
  side you clicked on and reappear on the other list. If you add SIGs to
  the right side, you will begin to get messages for that SIG. If you
  add SIGs to the left side, you will no longer receive messages for those
  SIGs.

  Just select ACCEPT when you are satisfied with the changes. The next time
  you logon to VBBS and select SIGs, you will receive any new messages for
  the list of SIGs you indicated above.

  If you select Change SIGs before logging onto a VBBS BBS and selecting
  SIGs, you will receive an error message 'Bad directory. See doc files'.
  This message means you need to logon to a VBBS BBS and select SIGs from
  the main menu. After getting the 'SIG Complete' message from Term, you
  then should be able to select Change SIGs and get a valid directory.

                                                    Ian
